    <string name="forward_incoming_desc">Bridge incoming cellular calls to your SIP server</string>
    <string name="speakerphone_loopback">Speakerphone loopback (audio fix)</string>
    <string name="speakerphone_loopback_desc">Forces the speakerphone on and routes SIP audio through the device speaker so the cellular call\'s microphone picks it up. Use this if callers can\'t hear audio. Causes echo and lower quality — only enable if needed. Restart gateway after changing.</string>
    <string name="mute_device_mic">Mute device microphone</string>
    <string name="mute_device_mic_desc">Gateway mode: cellular caller hears ONLY SIP audio (e.g. FreePBX announcements), not ambient room noise from the device microphone. Turn off only if someone is actually speaking into this phone.</string>
    <string name="block_mic_system_wide">Block microphone system-wide</string>
    <string name="block_mic_system_wide_desc">Hard kill switch (Android 12+). Same state as Quick Settings → Mic access. ALL apps see silence — cellular calls, voice assistants, recorders, voice typing, everything. On supported Pixels this is a hardware-level disconnect at the audio codec. Persists across reboots and Copperhead being killed. The user can still toggle it off via Quick Settings. Emergency calls bypass it.</string>
    <string name="block_mic_unsupported">System mic block not available on this device / Android version</string>

